<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <!-- Main content -->
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>This extraordinary 11-day overland adventure traces the ancient Silk Road from China into the heart of Kyrgyzstan. Begin in Urumqi, travel through the fabled oasis city of Kashgar, then cross the remote Torugart Pass at 3,752 meters into a land of nomads, alpine lakes, and towering peaks. From the ancient caravanserai of Tash Rabat to the shores of Issyk Kul — the world's second-largest alpine lake — this journey reveals a side of the Silk Road few travelers ever experience.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Cross the Torugart Pass at 3,752m into Kyrgyzstan</li><li>Explore Kashgar's Sunday Market and Old City</li><li>Stay in a traditional yurt at Tash Rabat caravanserai</li><li>Experience nomadic life in Kochkor</li><li>Relax on the shores of Issyk Kul Lake</li><li>Visit the ancient Burana Tower near Bishkek</li><li>Taste Central Asian cuisine across two cultures</li><li>Journey along one of the Silk Road's most dramatic routes</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Urumqi</h4><p>Arrive in Urumqi, capital of Xinjiang. Transfer to your hotel. Evening visit to the Erdaoqiao Grand Bazaar — one of the largest markets in Central Asia. Welcome dinner with traditional Uyghur cuisine.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi ✈ Kashgar</h4><p>Morning visit to the Xinjiang Regional Museum to see the famous Tarim mummies. Afternoon flight to Kashgar, the legendary Silk Road trading city. Evening walk through the Old City — a living museum of Uyghur culture.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Market & Old City</h4><p>Experience the legendary Kashgar Sunday Market — a centuries-old trading hub where the Silk Road spirit lives on. Visit the Id Kah Mosque, the largest in China, and wander through the maze-like alleys of the Old City.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Karakoram Highway to Taxkorgan</h4><p>Drive the spectacular Karakoram Highway. Visit Karakul Lake at 3,600m with views of Muztagh Ata (7,546m). Arrive in Taxkorgan, China's westernmost town near the Tajikistan border.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Taxkorgan 3★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Taxkorgan — Stone Fort → Return to Kashgar</h4><p>Visit the ancient Stone Fort and pristine grasslands. Return to Kashgar via the Karakoram Highway with stunning mountain scenery. Free evening for last-minute exploration.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar → Torugart Pass → Tash Rabat (Kyrgyzstan)</h4><p>Early morning departure for the Torugart Pass border crossing at 3,752m. After immigration formalities, descend into the dramatic landscapes of Kyrgyzstan. Arrive at Tash Rabat — a remarkably preserved 15th-century stone caravanserai nestled in a mountain valley. Overnight in a traditional yurt camp.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏕️ Yurt Camp</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tash Rabat → Kochkor</h4><p>Explore the Tash Rabat caravanserai in the morning light. Drive through the scenic Tian Shan Mountains to Kochkor — a village known for its traditional felt carpet (shyrdak) workshops. Meet local artisans and try your hand at felt-making.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Guesthouse</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kochkor — Issyk Kul Lake</h4><p>Drive to the southern shore of Issyk Kul, the "Warm Lake" — the world's second-largest alpine lake after Titicaca. En route, visit the ancient petroglyphs at Cholpon-Ata. Afternoon free to swim or walk along the shore.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Issyk Kul 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Issyk Kul — Free Day</h4><p>Full day at leisure on the shores of Issyk Kul. Options include hiking in the surrounding mountains, boat trips, visiting local fish markets, or simply relaxing on the beach. This is your day to unwind in one of Central Asia's most beautiful settings.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Issyk Kul 4★</span><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Issyk Kul → Burana Tower → Bishkek</h4><p>Drive to Bishkek, Kyrgyzstan's leafy capital. En route, visit the Burana Tower — an 11th-century minaret and the last remnant of the ancient Silk Road city of Balasagun. Afternoon city tour of Bishkek: Ala-Too Square, Osh Bazaar, and the White House.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Bishkek 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Bishkek</h4><p>Free time until your airport transfer. Your epic overland Silk Road adventure concludes in Bishkek. До свидания!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's Included</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>10 nights accommodation (hotels + yurt + guesthouse)</p></div>
